      {
        "id": "def-root-height-completion-for-weightwise-quasi-r-intertwiners",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "The root-height completion for weightwise quasi-$R$ intertwiners",
        "deps": [
          "def-the-bar-lattice-and-integral-lattice-of-a-based-module",
          "def-positive-negative-and-toral-quantum-subalgebras",
          "lem-lusztig-and-kashiwara-normalizations-match-by-root-color"
        ],
        "statement": "For the fixed library coproduct use the diagonal root-height completion C_hat=\u220f_(nu\u2208Q+)U^+[nu]\u2297U^-[-nu], with multiplication (AB)_nu=\u03a3_(beta+gamma=nu)A_beta B_gamma. Each component sum is finite because I is finite and root coefficients are nonnegative integers. For intertwining with \u0394U, use the ambient completed tensor square obtained from Lusztig4.1.1 by the actual v=q^-1, K_h\u21a6K_-h presentation map and tensor flip; equivalently all generator identities are read coefficientwise in the root grading. The tensor orientation is POSITIVE first, NEGATIVE second.\nA family acts on m_mu\u2297n_eta by its finite sum whenever U^+_nu m_mu\u2297U^-_-nu n_eta vanishes for all sufficiently high nu. This holds if the first factor has finite-union bounded-above support, or if the second factor is a lowest module with bounded-below support. For both factors in finite-weight-space O_int the relevant fixed total-weight subspace is finite dimensional, and every tail beyond a finite degree acts0 there. An infinite series is not evaluated on a two-sided-unbounded pair without this explicit finiteness condition. This completion and \u0398_0=1 are field-level data; no universal-R, braiding or integral coefficient property is asserted here.",
