        "statement": "Let B_K be the normalized Kashiwara half form and let \u03b9:U^+\u2192U^- send E_i\u21a6F_i (equivalently use the library's signed Chevalley involution with the compensating degree sign). For x of positive degree nu and y of negative degree\u2212nu define D(x,y)=d_nu^-1 B_K(\u03b9x,y), d_nu=\u220f_i(q_i\u2212q_i^-1)^nu_i, and set different-degree pairings0. Then D(E_i,F_j)=delta_ij/(q_i\u2212q_i^-1), and D(E_i^(n),F_i^(n))=q_i^(\u2212n(n\u22121)/2)/([n]_i!(q_i\u2212q_i^-1)^n). The pairing with generator value1 is B_K transport, not this quasi-R/Drinfeld normalization. The completed normalized tensor uses the D-dual basis. On the simple-root Borel extensions its toral normalization is D(K_nu,K_mu)=q^((nu,mu)), with mixed toral/root generator pairings0 and counit normalization; the Hopf adjunction identities use \u0394 on the negative Borel and \u0394^op on the positive Borel. No unchosen pairing on arbitrary extra toral directions of Pvee is asserted.",
