        "statement": "For finite-dimensional V over Q(q), let M\u2282V be an A=Z[q,q^-1]-submodule spanning V and L0,L\u221e full free A0,A\u221e lattices. Write E=M\u2229L0\u2229L\u221e. (1) If E\u2192(M\u2229L0)/(M\u2229qL0) is a Z-isomorphism, then M\u2229L0\u2245Z[q]\u2297_Z E, M\u2229L\u221e\u2245Z[q^-1]\u2297_Z E and M\u2245A\u2297_Z E; the infinity residue map is also an isomorphism. Rational chart extension gives A0\u2297_Z E\u2245L0 and A\u221e\u2297_Z E\u2245L\u221e. If E has a finite Z-basis, these are actual free bases. No containment M\u2282L0\u2229L\u221e or freeness of M/E is assumed.\n(2) If a Z-module F maps into M\u2229L0\u2229L\u221e, generates M over A, and maps injectively into both rational residues L0/qL0 and L\u221e/q^-1L\u221e, then F\u2245E\u2245(M\u2229L0)/(M\u2229qL0).\n(3) More generally let N\u2282M be an A-submodule with integral balanced intersection E_N=N\u2229L0\u2229L\u221e. If a Z-module F maps to M\u2229(L0+N)\u2229(L\u221e+N), generates M modulo N over A, and maps injectively into (L0+Q N)/(qL0+Q N) and (L\u221e+Q N)/(q^-1L\u221e+Q N), then M is balanced. The sequence 0\u2192(N\u2229L0)/(N\u2229qL0)\u2192(M\u2229L0)/(M\u2229qL0)\u2192(L0+Q N)/(qL0+Q N) is exact, and the last image is the image of F. If F and E_N are finite free Z-modules, so is E_M, and M is free over A. These are Kashiwara91 Lemmas7.1.1\u20137.1.2, in integral notation; their rational base extension gives the usual Q[q\u00b1] criterion.",
        "strategy": "(1) E injects into the rational residue by the hypothesis, hence is Z-torsionfree. Residue surjectivity gives M\u2229L0\u2282\u03a3_(k=0)^n q^k E+M\u2229q^(n+1)L0 for every n, by repeatedly subtracting a lift and dividing by q (which preserves M). For x also in q^nL\u221e, the subtracted terms k\u2264n lie there; the remainder is in q^n(M\u2229qL0\u2229L\u221e)=0 by residue injectivity on E. Thus M\u2229L0\u2229q^nL\u221e=\u2295_(k=0)^n q^kE. Every element of M\u2229L0 has a finite infinity-pole bound, so the union over n gives Z[q]E. Distinct powers are independent: in a finite relation normalize the lowest exponent and reduce modulo q, then successively remove it. Also M=Z[q\u00b1](M\u2229L0) by finite zero-pole bounds. The analogous infinity-pole argument gives Z[q^-1]E and the mirror residue isomorphism. Since M spans V, Q(q)E spans V; rational residue injection shows a Q-basis of QE is independent and full. Expanding in that basis, zero/infinity valuation gives the full chart extension identities. Freeness over A is claimed only if E is actually finite free over Z.\n(2) Laurent expansions in phi(F) have unique finite coefficients: reduce the lowest exponent at0 using the first injection. If an expansion lies in L0 it has no negative exponent; if it lies in L\u221e it has no positive exponent, by the second injection. Therefore the intersection is exactly phi(F), with the claimed residue map and factorization. This is finite Laurent linear algebra, not passage to an unjustified formal limit.\n(3) Work first on each finitely generated submodule F\u2032 of F; its rational residue injection implies Z-torsionfreeness and hence finite Z-freeness. The balanced factorization of N gives N=(N\u2229L0)+(N\u2229L\u221e). If x\u2208M\u2229(L0+N)\u2229(L\u221e+N), subtract an element of N to put it in L0. Its remaining discrepancy from L\u221e lies in N; split that discrepancy into its zero and infinity chart parts, then subtract its zero chart part to obtain an element of M\u2229L0\u2229L\u221e. Thus the lifts of a finite Z-basis of F\u2032 can be changed by N so that they lie in the simultaneous intersection. Their direct sum with E_N injects into each rational residue: in the quotient modulo QN the F\u2032 component is forced0 by the assumed injection, and then E_N injectivity forces the remaining component0. They generate AF\u2032+N over A. Apply (2) to obtain balancedness and the exact residue sequence there. Taking the union over finite F\u2032 proves the general assertion, without claiming an infinite torsionfree Z-module is free. When F and E_N are finite free, the direct sum description gives E_M finite free. This reproduces the printed diagrams and avoids the native unsupported chart containment, wrong q^nL0/q^nL\u221e recursion and coherent-sheaf freeness shortcut.",
