        "statement": "For L_Z(infinity)=U_A^-\u2229L(infinity), its canonical injection L_Z/qL_Z\u2192L/qL has image exactly \u2295_(b\u2208B\u221e)Z b. It is a free Z-module with basis B\u221e and becomes the full rational crystal space after tensoring with Q. The normalized Kashiwara half form takes values on U_A^- in K_Z=Z[q,q^-1,(1\u2212q^(2n))^-1:n\u22651], and on L_Z in A_Z=Z[q,(1\u2212q^(2n))^-1:n\u22651]. Thus its residue pairing is Z-valued. Its coefficients in B\u221e are the integer pairings with b, and its norm1 elements are B\u221e\u222a(\u2212B\u221e). The operators e\u0303_i,f\u0303_i preserve L_Z and its integral residue subgroup. No A-module structure on L_Z, no equality with the rational residue as a Z-module, and no unsigned norm1 characterization is asserted. The module integral residue basis is established in globalization.",
        "strategy": "The integral skew-string supplier proves every string coefficient and both half Kashiwara operators preserve U_A^-. The completed crystal theorem proves their L\u221e stability. Consequently every lowering word applied to1 lies in L_Z, providing an integral representative of every b\u2208B\u221e. For P,Q in U_A^-, the exact divided-word denominator bound from the half form places B(P,Q) in K_Z: quantum factorial denominators are Laurent powers times products (1\u2212q^(2d_i r)) divided by powers (1\u2212q^(2d_i)), so K_Z contains every such value. This is the same normalized Kashiwara form as the q0 polarization; there is no second normalization factor between them. The post-grand-loop polarization lemma puts B(P,Q)\u2208A0 when P,Q\u2208L_Z. To prove A0\u2229K_Z=A_Z, take a common denominator D=\u220f(1\u2212q^(2n))^e with D(0)=1 and integer Laurent numerator. Regularity at0 says exactly that numerator has no negative powers. Evaluation of A_Z at0 gives integers. Thus, for any x\u2208L_Z with rational residue \u03a3 a_b b, pairing with the integral word representative of b gives a_b\u2208Z by orthonormality. Conversely all finite integer combinations of the representatives lie in L_Z. The kernel is qL_Z by the preceding Definition, proving the actual free integral residue quotient. For norm1, \u03a3 a_b\u00b2=1 with integers a_b has a single coefficient+1 OR\u22121, so the signed assertion follows. No global integral basis has been presumed.",
