        "statement": "For every symmetrizable datum in the explicitly chosen label-weight category, the triples (U_A^-,L\u221e,bar L\u221e) and (V_A(lambda),Llambda,bar Llambda) are integrally balanced componentwise. Their balanced Z-intersections map isomorphically to ZB\u221e and ZB\u03bb, respectively; after rational extension these maps identify with the full Q crystal spaces. The inverse lifts G\u221e(b),G\u03bb(b) are bar invariant. They form actual A=Z[q,q^-1] bases of the divided-power modules U_A^- and V_A(lambda), with finite free root/label components of ranks equal to their field dimensions (the half ranks are the classical PBW ranks).\nFor every i,n\u22651, I_(i,n)^A=\u2295_(b\u2208B\u221e\u2229f\u0303_i^nB\u221e)A G\u221e(b), and J_(i,n)^A=\u2295_(b\u2208B\u03bb\u2229f\u0303_i^nB\u03bb)A G\u03bb(b). In particular the module image ideal equals V_A\u2229F_i^n V; this saturation follows from the adapted global basis and is not an initial hypothesis. Under pi_lambda, G\u221e(b) maps to0 exactly when its crystal image is0 and otherwise to G\u03bb(pi(b)). All assertions are integral, general symmetrizable and proved without an integral-freeness premise. If e\u0303_i b=0 and n\u22651, then G\u221e(f\u0303_i^n b)\u2212F_i^(n)G\u221e(b) lies in I_(i,n+1)^A. This is the exact normalized top-string transition modulo the higher string ideal, not merely a modulo-q congruence.",
