module string ideal, in qLlambda and in bar Llambda; ideal balancedness forces it0. Likewise G_j(b)v=0. Hence their difference Q lies in U_A^-\u2229U^-F_k\u2229qL\u221e\u2229bar L\u221e. The local reversal supplier puts Qstar in U_A^-\u2229F_kU^-\u2229qL\u221e\u2229bar L\u221e. The already proved ordinary-power integral string extraction identifies U_A^-\u2229F_kU^-=I_(k,1)^A BEFORE this gluing step: the unique field position0 is zero and every extracted positive top coefficient is integral. Therefore Qstar is in I_(k,1)^A\u2229qL\u221e\u2229bar L\u221e, which is0 by the height-r string-ideal balance. Thus Q=0. This is the actual printed Kashiwara91 Lemma7.5.1 gluing argument, including its right-ideal/kernel and signed-star hypotheses.\nEvery positive-height crystal word has a lowering predecessor. Define G\u221e(b) by any available string lift; gluing makes it independent. Since U_A^- in this degree is \u03a3_i I_(i,1)^A (each divided-word generator has a first negative color), the free string-ideal bases give U_A^-=A\u00b7\u03a3_b ZG\u221e(b). These lifts inject into both rational chart residues: at0 they give the basis b, and at infinity their bar invariance gives the corresponding bar basis. Apply the integral chart generation lemma with the finite free Z-module F=\u03a3ZG\u221e(b). It gives balancedness, the Z-balanced intersection, the A-basis and both chart bases. Each I_(i,n) lift now equals the full G\u221e lift by uniqueness, proving its adapted basis and Z membership.\nFor a module, if pi(b)=0 choose i with e\u0303_i b\u22600. Its half lift lies in I_(i,1), so G\u221e(b)v lies in J_(i,1), qLlambda and bar Llambda; the already proved module ideal balance forces it0 (Kashiwara91 Lemma7.5.2). Surviving images are bar fixed, have residue pi(b), and these residues biject onto B\u03bb by the completed grand loop. They span V_A because pi(U_A^-)=V_A and the killed images are0. The finite free Z-span of surviving images injects into both rational residues; the chart generation lemma gives module balancedness and its actual A-basis. Uniqueness identifies these images with G\u03bb. Ideal lifts then agree with the corresponding module G\u03bb; their field scalar extensions span precisely F_i^n V. The direct free decomposition of V_A by all G\u03bb therefore proves J_(i,n)=V_A\u2229F_i^n V as a conclusion. This also proves the integral module residue subgroup is ZB\u03bb.\nThe induction closes in every finite component. Global direct sums give integral bases with field ranks, and the published generic/classical half-rank supplier identifies the PBW ranks, carrying its existing AC hypothesis. No dot-U basis, rational-Q PID proof, false A-module residue, arbitrary torsionfree-to-free assertion, or chart containment assumption is used. The top-string transition is part of the integral chart extension step: its new residue lift is obtained from phi_b=F_i^(n)G\u221e(b) by subtracting an element of the higher ideal N=I_(i,n+1)^A to put it in both charts. The resulting integral balanced lift is uniquely G\u221e(f\u0303_i^n b). Thus their difference is in N exactly. The same fact holds in every module string image. This explicit transition supplies the signed-basis positive-recursion dictionary used by the canonical comparison.",
