        "statement": "For the divided-power integral form $U_A^-$ of [[def-lusztig-divided-power-integral-form]] and for every dominant $\\lambda$, let $M_A$ be $U_A^-$ or $V_A(\\lambda)=U_A^-v_\\lambda$, let $L$ be $\\mathcal L(\\infty)$ or $\\mathcal L(\\lambda)$ with bar lattice $L^-=\\psi(L)$, and let $\\mathcal B$ be $\\mathcal B(\\infty)$ or $\\mathcal B(\\lambda)$. Then there is a unique lower global family $G(\\mathcal B)\\subseteq M_A\\cap L\\cap L^-$ with the property that the residue class of $G(b)$ in $(M_A\\cap L)/(M_A\\cap qL)$ is $b$ for every $b\\in\\mathcal B$, namely the family of [[def-lower-global-basis-of-a-quantum-highest-weight-module]]. It is bar invariant, a genuine $A=\\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]$ basis of $M_A$, and a basis of both rational chart lattices $L$ and $L^-$ over $A_0$ and $A_\\infty$; its $\\mathbb Z$-span is the simultaneous balanced intersection $M_A\\cap L\\cap L^-$ and its field span is the whole module. It is adapted to every divided string-image ideal in the exact sense of the integral balanced theorem, and the same family is obtained with residue $b$ over either chart. No word family is assumed to be a basis, no unitriangular characterization is used, and no lower lattice self-duality is asserted.",
