        "statement": "Let M=\u2295_mu M_mu be U^- or V(lambda), with finite root/label components, lower global A-lattice M_A=\u2295_b A G(b), rational lower charts L0 and L\u221e=bar L0, and the normalized homogeneous Kashiwara half or highest-module polarization B. Define its RESTRICTED graded integral form-dual by M_A^vee=\u2295_mu{x\u2208M_mu:B(x,(M_A)_mu)\u2282A}. Define dual rational charts L0^vee={x:B(x,L0)\u2282A0} and L\u221e^vee={x:B(x,L\u221e)\u2282A\u221e}, also as restricted direct sums. The upper global family is the unique homogeneous field family G^up(b) with B(G(b\u2032),G^up(b))=delta_(b,b\u2032). Its existence and actual dual-lattice bases/perfection are proved by the next theorem.\nThe upper bar is the B-adjoint semilinear involution psi^vee determined by B(psi u,psi^vee v)=overline{B(u,v)}. Upper Kashiwara operators are e\u0303_i^up=(f\u0303_i^low)^adj and f\u0303_i^up=(e\u0303_i^low)^adj, defined componentwise by the nondegenerate finite-dimensional form. They are distinct from the lower operators in general. The upper zero chart is the dual chart L0^vee; post-grand-loop perfection identifies it with L0, but the upper infinity chart L\u221e^vee is not automatically the lower bar chart L\u221e. The exact assertions of the following theorem are weightwise perfect A-duality, dual globalization in these genuine dual charts, and crystal compatibility for the respective adjoint operators. No full product Hom_A(M_A,A) identification, lower A-self-duality, ordinary-bar fixedness or unqualified upper/lower operator equality is asserted.",
