        ],
        "statement": "For every finite root/label component of M=U^- or V(lambda), the restricted integral dual M_A^vee has the actual A-basis {G^up(b)} dual to {G(b)}, and B:(M_A^vee)_mu\u00d7(M_A)_mu\u2192A is perfect. Globally these bases form direct sums; this means restricted graded perfectness, not identification with the full product Hom_A(M_A,A).\nThe dual charts are L0^vee=\u2295A0G^up(b) and L\u221e^vee=\u2295A\u221eG^up(b), and their balanced Z-intersection is \u2295ZG^up(b). Thus the dual triple is integrally balanced. At0, L0^vee=L0 and G^up(b) has residue b; at infinity its residue is the dual of the lower infinity-chart class in the dual infinity chart. The upper bar psi^vee fixes each G^up(b). The upper operators satisfy EXACT mixed adjunction B(f\u0303^low u,v)=B(u,e\u0303^up v), B(e\u0303^low u,v)=B(u,f\u0303^up v). Their reductions at0 equal the lower crystal operators and give the same crystal set B.\nFor a divided module string F_i^(n)v of top rank-one weight a, put d_(a,n)=q_i^(n(a\u2212n))[a choose n]_i. Then e\u0303_i^up at position n\u22651 multiplies the preceding divided position by d_(a,n)/d_(a,n\u22121)=q_i^(a\u22122n+1)[a\u2212n+1]_i/[n]_i, and f\u0303_i^up at position n<a multiplies the next by its reciprocal d_(a,n)/d_(a,n+1). For a half string with e_i\u2032v=0, put d_n=q_i^(\u2212n(n\u22121)/2)/[n]_i!=1/[n]_(q_i\u00b2)!; the corresponding ratios are d_n/d_(n\u22121)=1/[n]_(q_i\u00b2) and d_n/d_(n+1)=[n+1]_(q_i\u00b2). All admissible ratios are units\u22611 in A0. Consequently unweighted lower adjunction holds modulo q, but generally not exactly over Q(q). No equality of upper and lower integral bases, even in symmetric type, is implied.",
        "strategy": "Fix a finite component and its already-proved lower A-basis g_b=G(b). The field Gram matrix C=(B(g_b,g_c)) is invertible over Q(q), not asserted invertible over A. Define g_b^up using C^-1. For any x in the component, its coordinates in this dual field basis are exactly B(g_b,x). Hence x is in M_A^vee iff those coordinates are in A. This proves its genuine free A-basis and the perfect pairing with M_A, by the evaluation matrices delta; no A-unit determinant or lower self-duality is required. This is a finite proof in each degree, extended only by restricted direct sums.\nThe lower chart lattices have bases g_b over A0 and A\u221e by integral globalization. The same coefficient criterion proves their dual chart bases g_b^up over the corresponding rings. Their triple intersection is Z-span because A\u2229A0\u2229A\u221e=Z. The exact integral dual globalization follows, with Q extension at each rational residue. Existing post-grand-loop Gram perfection identifies L0^vee=L0, and B(g_b,g_c)\u2261delta at0 implies g_b^up\u2261b there. At infinity, pairing with the lower infinity basis defines the actual dual residue; it does not assert congruence modulo q^-1 in the LOWER infinity lattice. Since psi g_b=g_b, the definition B(psi u,psi^vee v)=overline B(u,v) gives psi^vee g_b^up=g_b^up and transports the two dual charts.\nFor exact operators, extract finite divided strings. Different positions with different highest components are orthogonal: repeated E_i or e_i\u2032 adjunction leaves a highest vector paired with a positive F_i power, hence0; at equal position the pairing is d_(a,n) or d_n times the top-component form. Therefore the adjoint of the normalized lower shift has precisely the displayed norm ratio, proving the exact MIXED adjunction. The module ratio equals (1\u2212q_i^(2(a\u2212n+1)))/(1\u2212q_i^(2n)) after factoring powers, a unit with constant1 for 1\u2264n\u2264a. The half ratios are the displayed ordinary q_i\u00b2 quantum integers and reciprocals, also units\u22611. Thus the upper operators preserve L0, reduce to the same crystal actions and satisfy the same partial-inverse edge property. This is Kashiwara91\u00a72.4\u2019s distinction between lower and upper operators, combined with its\u00a75.1 A0-perfection and the constructed global bases. No star-invariance argument is substituted for form-duality, no rank-one check is promoted to a general proof, and no full infinite-rank algebraic dual is invoked.",
