        "statement": "In rank one the lower global/canonical vectors are exactly F_i^(n), bar fixed and congruent to their normalized crystal classes. Their Kashiwara norms are1/[n]_(q_i\u00b2)!, while the transported Lusztig norms are1/\u220f_(r=1)^n(1\u2212q_i^(2r)); the full color factor is(1\u2212q_i\u00b2)^\u2212n. Ordinary F_i^n differs by the nonunit symmetric factorial, and Drinfeld generator normalization includes(q_i\u2212q_i^-1)^\u22121. This explicitly matches, rather than conflates, the four conventions.\nIn type A2 degree alpha1+alpha2, the two lower global/canonical vectors are EXACTLY F1F2,F2F1, with no triangular correction. Their Kashiwara Gram matrix is[[1,q],[q,1]], already identity moduloq, and their transported Lusztig Gram is(1\u2212q\u00b2)^\u22122 times this matrix. The Kashiwara upper dual vectors are(1\u2212q\u00b2)^\u22121(F1F2\u2212qF2F1) and(1\u2212q\u00b2)^\u22121(F2F1\u2212qF1F2); they are not the lower vectors. Lusztig form-duals are further multiplied by(1\u2212q\u00b2)^2. In degree2alpha1 the lower vector isF1^(2), with the rank-one norm. These computations exhibit the actual convention dictionary and make no false Gram-unimodularity or unspecified correction claim.",
        "strategy": "Rank one is the unique divided string of1; the corrected balanced theorem gives exactly the divided lower lift, and the already-derived degree-color recursion gives both norms and the Drinfeld scalar. In degree alpha1+alpha2 there is no Serre relation, and e_1\u2032F2=e_2\u2032F1=0. Thus f\u03031f\u03032\u00b71=F1F2 and f\u03032f\u03031\u00b71=F2F1, integral/bar fixed with distinct crystal residues. Balanced uniqueness gives them as the exact lifts. Adjunction computes the two diagonals1 and the cross term q (e_1\u2032(F2F1)=qF2), proving the displayed Gram matrix and determinant1\u2212q\u00b2. Its field inverse gives the two genuine Kashiwara upper duals, not an A-unit inverse. The form dictionary multiplies Gram by(1\u2212q\u00b2)^\u22122 and therefore multiplies dual vectors by its reciprocal. The q0 residues of lower and upper agree, while their A lattices generally differ. The lower degree2alpha1 norm is the exact rank-one1/(1+q\u00b2). All displayed finite calculations are complete and consistent with the full canonical comparison supplier.",
