        ],
        "statement": "In V(omega)=L_1(1), let v be highest and w=Fv, with Ev=0,Fv=w,Ew=v,Fw=0,Kv=qv,Kw=q^-1w. Then V_A=Av\u2295Aw, L0=A0v\u2295A0w, L\u221e=A\u221ev\u2295A\u221ew and E_Z=Zv\u2295Zw. The integral globalization maps E_Z isomorphically onto the Z-span of its two crystal classes; its rational extension gives the full Q residue. Its lower global basis is v,w. The field string image FV is Q(q)w, its integral image ideal is Aw and its balanced part is Zw.\nOn V\u2297V the exact quasi-R is1+(q\u2212q^-1)E\u2297F. Hence \u03a8(vv)=vv, \u03a8(vw)=vw, \u03a8(wv)=wv+(q\u2212q^-1)vw, \u03a8(ww)=ww, using concatenation for tensor notation. This preserves total weight and the A tensor lattice and is a semilinear involution. The actual tensor global basis is vv,vw,wv+qvw,ww; raw wv is not bar fixed. Its zero crystal lattice is the A0 tensor lattice and its balanced Z-part is the Z-span of these corrected vectors.\nFor the mixed free lattice L\u2032=A0(v+w)\u2295qA0v with actual infinity chart bar L\u2032=A\u221e(v+w)\u2295q^-1A\u221ev, the integral balanced part is only Z(v+w); it misses the valid residue class of qv. Thus it is genuinely nonbalanced, although v+w is bar fixed. L\u2032 is not claimed to be a crystal lattice.",
        "strategy": "A\u2229A0=Z[q], A\u2229A\u221e=Z[q^-1] and A\u2229A0\u2229A\u221e=Z give the stated balanced parts; q is a unit in A, so A/qA is0 and is never used for the residue. The two chart residues are treated through Z[q]/qZ[q]=Z. Divided powers ofF on this module give only v,w and the higher ones vanish, proving the exact integral lattice. The string-image field/A/Z spaces are distinguished.\nThe correct generator-normalized field \u0398_alpha=(q\u2212q^-1)E\u2297F is proved by intertwining, not by c+barc=0 alone. Equivalently applying \u0394E\u0398=\u0398bar\u0394E to ww gives q vw+wv on the left and q^-1vw+wv+c vw on the right, forcing c=q\u2212q^-1. The map E\u2297F sends wv tovw and kills vv,vw,ww, so the four formulas and total-weight preservation follow. Bar twice cancels c+barc=0, verifying involutivity after the scalar is fixed. Directly \u03a8(wv+qvw)=wv+(q\u2212q^-1)vw+q^-1vw=wv+qvw. The other three vectors are fixed; their A-transition matrix is unitriangular and their q0 residues are the raw tensor basis, giving the stated global and chart bases.\nPut a=v+w,t=v, so V_A=Aa\u2295At. In the mixed zero chart the t coefficient has order\u22651, while in the ACTUAL bar chart it has infinity order\u22651, i.e. Laurent degree\u2264\u22121. No nonzero integer Laurent polynomial satisfies both, so E\u2032=Za. Its integral zero residue has independent generators a,qv, and E\u2032 misses exactly the latter. The non-crystal assertions follow from e\u0303a=v\u2209L\u2032 and its two weight intersections qA0v,qA0w. No nonexistent class v+qL\u2032 is used.",
